From 7657907486bf0ff585d75659bb7fa14b1a7700d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virt-ios <virt-ios@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:12:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] :new: Build the C library on Windows

The whole library builds for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc with the vulkan
feature: reims-vgpu-c, reims-vgpu, reims-vgpu-window and the Vulkan crate.

- reims-vgpu-window: the SDL3 window serves Windows too (native/linux is
  SDL's, not Linux's); the control socket is Unix-only and logged off.
- reims-graphics (x86-64 macOS guests: a BAR region, a doorbell fd) is a
  Unix-only dependency. On Windows the C API keeps its constants, types
  and functions (graphics_windows.rs) and rvg_graphics_device_create
  answers RVG_ERR_UNSUPPORTED, so hosts link unchanged.
- reims-vgpu: DefaultPlatform is VulkanPlatform on Windows; KVM's dirty
  log answers no slot off Linux; graphics_video is Unix-only; the window's
  swapchain sink is built on Windows.
- reims-vgpu-c: a memory range file's fd is the section HANDLE on Windows
  (handles are 32-bit significant), duplicated with DuplicateHandle into
  a winvm::Section; its size is not checked (no public call reads it);
  ffi's catch is std's catch_unwind, as on Linux.

Verified: cargo check -p reims-vgpu-c --features vulkan on Windows,
0 errors. Not yet: the static library for QEMU (windows-gnu), tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
